description:
FILED s536c (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from #1611's acceptance run of YAML-PP t/54.glob.t: with #1611 fixed the file's subtest `valid` passes WHOLE (11 rows; on c950ad43 it stopped after 4 on Test::Deep's hijacked `hash`), and subtest `ioscalar` then dies "Can't use an undefined value as a SCALAR reference".  PRE-EXISTING (c950ad43 answers the same).

YAML::PP::Schema::Perl::represent_glob reads every slot `my $value = *{ $glob }{ $type }` and does `$value = $$value` for SCALAR.  perl's SCALAR slot always exists (`*x{SCALAR}` is a reference to the possibly-undef scalar, created on demand); PCL answers undef for a slot nothing wrote:

    use Symbol;
    our $x;
    print "1 ", ref(*{\*main::x}{SCALAR}), "\n";
    print "2 ", ref(*{\*main::never_used}{SCALAR}), "\n";
    my $g3 = gensym; print "3 ", ref(*{$g3}{SCALAR}), "\n";
    print "4 ", ref(*main::nothere{SCALAR}), "\n";
      perl 5.40.3: 1 SCALAR / 2 SCALAR / 3 SCALAR / 4 SCALAR
      PCL (base c950ad43 and s536c): 1 SCALAR / 2 / 3 / 4      (silent: an empty string)

IO::File->new returns a Symbol::gensym glob, so `*{$fh}{SCALAR}` is undef and the deref dies.  The NEXT slot in the same loop is #3674 (`*{$fh}{IO}` answers GLOB where perl answers the IO::File object), so the file reaches `like $dump, qr{--- !perl/glob:IO::File}` only after both.

FIX SHAPE (not built): the glob-slot reader for SCALAR vivifies the slot's container (as perl's gv_fetchpv GV_ADD does for the SV slot) and answers a reference to it -- check `p-glob-slot` / the `*x{THING}` arm; the ARRAY / HASH slots keep perl's "undef until used" answer (#1117 has that half).  ROWS: YAML-PP-v0.39.0-0 t/54.glob.t *PLAN* (re-keyed from #4104 by s536c).

=== DONE (s536g) ===
`p-glob-slot`'s SCALAR arm answered NIL for an unbound slot symbol; it now binds the package scalar (a fresh box) and answers a reference to it, as perl's gv_fetchpv GV_ADD makes the SV slot of every glob.  ARRAY / HASH / CODE unchanged (undef until used; probed).  perl = tree on 20 probe lines: `*{\*main::never_used}{SCALAR}`, `*{gensym}{SCALAR}`, `*main::nothere{SCALAR}`, `*$fh{SCALAR}` of a lexical handle, `*{IO::File->new(...)}{SCALAR}`, `*STDOUT{SCALAR}`, a write through it, two reads giving the same ref.  The IO slot of an IO::File glob still answers GLOB where perl answers IO::File (#3674).  YAML-PP-v0.39.0-0 t/54.glob.t one-file run: 3/3 = perl (PLAN 3); its *PLAN* row left baselines/cpan-board14-fails.tsv by edit (CLOSE-WITH-ROWS; Pl/t/verdict-register-01.t PASS).  Guard Pl/t/glob-slot-operand-01.t row 9 (fails on ba7863a3).  ir-spec §8.  Commit 67888f1e (rebased onto MAIN-READY-81 = s532c's glob work before the edit, rule 34).


